### Initialize GLTFLoader and Create Async Load Function

Source: https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/blob/dev/manual/examples/cleanup-loaded-files.html

This snippet initializes a `GLTFLoader` instance, which is used to load 3D models in the GLTF format into the Three.js scene. It also defines a `loadGLTF` helper function that wraps the loader's asynchronous `load` method in a Promise. This allows for easier integration with `async/await` patterns, simplifying the handling of model loading operations.

```javascript
const gltfLoader = new GLTFLoader();

function loadGLTF( url ) {
  return new Promise( ( resolve, reject ) => {
    gltfLoader.load( url, resolve, undefined, reject );
  } );
}
```

